      "standardized_narrative": "The Syndicate's gross claims outstanding at the start of 2019 were $485.327m. During 2019 gross prior-year provisions were strengthened by $132.679m (27.35% of opening gross reserves), driven principally by loss creep and adverse development from prior natural catastrophe events - notably typhoon Jebi (2018) and hurricane Irma (2017) - with the most material deterioration attributed to Jebi. Some prior-year improvement was noted on the Aviation account which partially offset losses. The figure is taken from the Technical Provisions 'Change in prior year provisions' gross column.",
